  description: "Blightstool was once a harmless fungal culture engineered to recycle
    biological waste. Exposure to unstable E-Core radiation caused the organism to
    develop neural clusters and aggressive growth patterns. It now spreads by releasing
    corrosive spores that rewrite nearby organic matter. Researchers believe Blightstool
    no longer follows any natural survival instinct\u2014only expansion."
